  <h2 id="semantics">A concrete correction: domain and range</h2>
  <p>
    Source-method ODR-0014 retired on 28 August 2026 an earlier convention that treated
    repeated RDFS domains as alternatives when inference was disabled. Its 30 August
    amendment added complete, exclusive applicability coverage and governed waivers.
    Under <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-schema/#ch_domain">standard RDFS semantics</a>,
    repeated domains imply membership in all declared classes. Choosing not to run
    that inference locally does not change what the exported vocabulary says.
  </p>
  <p>
    The normative method keeps <code>rdfs:domain</code> and <code>rdfs:range</code> for
    universally intended implications; <code>schema:domainIncludes</code> and
    <code>schema:rangeIncludes</code> express alternative intended uses. SHACL describes
    the validation requirements. OPDA ODR-0027 R5 and the older ODR-0032/0033 documentary
    account preserve the earlier convention. They explain historical implementation,
    not an exception to W3C semantics or the current source-method rule.
  </p>
  <p>
    The same distinction applies to SSSOM: the earlier OPDA deferral does not describe
    the now-selected mapping method. A required mapping-record discipline and an empty
    current candidate mapping register can coexist. This website update records the
    normative direction; it does not rewrite the ontology corpus, invent mapping
    records or claim a completed generator migration.
  </p>

  <h2 id="legacy">What the legacy PDTF explanations contribute</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/concepts-and-architecture/modelling-frameworks">legacy modelling explainer</a>,
    <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/concepts-and-architecture/identity">identity and classification guide</a>
    and generated concept pages provide useful worked examples. They remain
    explanations of the schema-derived model. Their specific identity criteria,
    technical counts and runtime conventions do not automatically define a new
    context's model. We carry forward the reasoning, test it against property work
    and apply the current normative decisions.
  </p>
